# Everything in here is generated from credentials, so nothing is committed
# unless it is explicitly allowed below. Deny-by-default: a file added later
# lands on the ignored side on its own, which is what you want in a dotfiles
# repo that gets pushed.
#
# Kept out on purpose:
#   config.json          every proxy password, uuid and the VPN login
#   subscription.url     the subscription token
#   subscription.json    the downloaded node list, passwords included
#   vpn/device/          CyberGhost device identity: private key, certificate,
#                        and the username/password that match its CN
#
# Safe to publish: generate.py rebuilds all of the above from those inputs,
# and countries.txt is just a list of ISO codes.

*
!.gitignore
!generate.py
!vpn/
vpn/*
!vpn/countries.txt
